  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Ciclobendazole is a benzimidazole compound classified as an antinematodal anthelmintic, meaning it was intended for treating worm (nematode) infections. It appears to be only an experimental chemical entity, with no authorised marketing in the European Union, so its current use is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q383730&quot;>Wikidata Q383730</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>ciclobendazole</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>P02CA04</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13465&quot;>DB13465</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/35803&quot;>35803</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:135067&quot;>135067</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q383730&quot;>Q383730</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C13H13N3O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>259.265 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
